<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49104" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρην-έω</span></b> , fut.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ήσω</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					1541
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				632
			</span></i> (lyr.): aor. 1
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ησα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Tr.</u>
					[111]
				</span></i>
			:—
				Med.
			 (v. infr. <i><span class="en">
				2
			</span></i>): impers. in pf.
			
				Pass.
			 (v. infr.): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θρῆνος</span>):—<i>sing a dirge, wail</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοῦσαι δ᾽ ἐννέα πᾶσαι ἀμειβόμεναι
					ὀπὶ καλῇ θρήνεον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					24.61
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ὁ θρηνήσων</span>; <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
			</span></i> l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς . . ἔσθ᾽ ὁ
			θρηνῶν</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Nu.</u>
				1260
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. πρὸς τύμβον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ch.</u>
					926
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. καὶ ὀδύρεσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					38d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς σφᾶς αὐτούς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					8.128
				</span></i>
			: c.acc.cogn., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στονόεσσαν ἀοιδὴν . .
				ἐθρήνεον</span>
			<i>were singing</i> a doleful dirge, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				24.7221
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γόον θ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				291
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀξυτόνους ᾠδάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Aj.</u>
				</span></i>
			l.c.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπῳδάς</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				582
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕμνους</span>, of the
			nightingale, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Av.</u>
				211
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φθόγγους ἀλύρους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					162.7
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅλις μοι τεθρήνηται γόοις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					1401
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱκανῶς τεθρήνηται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Cat.</u>
					20
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.acc.,
				<i>bewail</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. πόνους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					615
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν θάνατον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Phd.</u>
					85a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅσα τὸν . . ἐμὸν θρηνῶ πατέρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.
					<u>El.</u>
					94
				</span></i>
			 (anap.), cf. <i><span class="en">
				530
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ev.Luc.</u>
				23.27
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸν φύντα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					449
				</span></i>
			:—so also 
				Med.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄκος γὰρ οὐδὲν τόνδε θρηνεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					43
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be lamented</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				852
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Fr.</u>
				653
			</span></i>.</div>
